// Explicit struct alignment is refused, and must stay refused until a backend
// can carry the alignment in its canonical target data layout.
//
// `align(N)` raises a type's minimum alignment. Lowering decides that layout,
// so accepting the declaration before the layout work exists would run every
// user of this type at the natural alignment and silently discard the request.
// This case pins the current explicit rejection so the gate cannot be opened by
// accident; promoting it to acceptance requires the alignment implementation
// and a positive test in the same change.
struct Aligned16 align(16) {
    value: i64
}
print(1)
